<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Launcher background colour.

  This is the ORANGE of the logo's outer rim, sampled from the artwork rather than
  chosen: `#F58551` is what a radial scan reads at eight angles across the rim band.

  It was `#FFFFFF` when the icon showed a cropped disc, because the disc sat on a
  lavender field and white was merely a placeholder. That is no longer the artwork.
  The logo is now the full framed roundel, whose outermost edge is an orange rim, so a
  background that does not match it shows as a halo of a second colour around the
  edge wherever the launcher's mask crops inside the circle.

  Matching the rim means the roundel has no visible boundary against its own
  background: the mask shape cuts into the orange and the icon reads as one solid
  orange field carrying the roundel detail.

  A NOTE ON DOUBLE HYPHENS: AAPT2 rejects a double hyphen anywhere inside an XML
  comment, which is why no CSS custom property name is written literally in this file.
  The build fails on it rather than warning, and the error reports a character column
  rather than the file, so it is worth knowing before editing.
-->
<resources>
    <color name="ic_launcher_background">#F58551</color>
</resources>